feat(server): land M3-P1 production capabilities (multi-dim rate limit + load shed + TLS/mTLS/FIPS + livez/readyz + access log)

* Multi-dimensional rate limiter: per-Origin (regex unlimited list),
  per-IP (CIDR trust list), per-Target-Host and Global token buckets,
  all backed by governor's lock-free GCRA. The first dimension to fail
  wins so we attribute rejections to the most specific cause via the
  corx_rate_limited_total{dimension} counter.
* Load-shed middleware: when rate_limit.global.inflight_max > 0, an
  atomic counter on ServerBuild rejects excess concurrency with
  503 Service Unavailable + Retry-After: 1 and bumps the same counter
  under dimension="global".
* TLS/mTLS/FIPS: new corx-server::tls module compiles a rustls
  ServerConfig from the operator's cert / key / optional client CA,
  advertises ALPN (default h2 / http/1.1), and serves via axum-server
  with the same graceful-shutdown signal as the cleartext path. mtls
  is feature-gated; fips flips the rustls provider to aws-lc-rs through
  corx-core/fips.
* Health probes: /livez (bare process liveness) and /readyz (drains to
  503 once a shutdown signal flips ServerBuild::ready). /healthz is
  kept as an alias of /readyz for k8s default probes.
* Graceful shutdown v2: shutdown_signal flips ready immediately on
  SIGTERM/Ctrl+C so load balancers stop routing while in-flight
  requests drain.
* Access log: corx::access event per completed request with method,
  path, status, duration_ms, client_ip, origin, request_id, error_kind,
  layered at the outermost position so it captures timeouts and
  load-shed responses.
* Two-stage RequestGuard (check_origin then check_rate) so the
  per-target-host bucket sees the validated punycode hostname.

BREAKING CHANGE: RateLimitConfig flattened single-bucket schema replaced
with four nested sub-configs (origin / ip / target_host / global).
TlsConfig gains client_ca_path and alpn_protocols. shutdown::run now
takes Arc<AtomicBool> ready flag.

68 unit tests passing across the workspace with --all-features.
